.TH CS2BLOCKCTL 1 "2026-11-11" "cs2blocker 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cs2blockctl \- manage CS2 SDR datacenter blocking rules
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cs2blockctl
[\fB\-\-sudo\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B cs2blockctl
\fB\-\-version\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cs2blockctl
lists CS2 SDR POPs, selects datacenters, and applies host firewall rules.
Privileged changes are performed by a small helper through
.BR pkexec (1)
and a polkit action, or through
.BR sudo (8)
with \fB\-\-sudo\fR.
.PP
The tool manages exactly one nftables table,
.IR "inet cs2blocker" ,
or a single
.I CS2BLOCKER
iptables chain when the fallback backend is selected. It does not touch the
game, Steam, or other firewall objects. The default rule drops SDR UDP traffic
only; ICMP remains reachable.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-sudo
Use \fBsudo\fR instead of \fBpkexec\fR for privileged commands.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show command help and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list [\-\-region REGION] [\-\-json]
List POPs, regions, relay counts and port ranges. This command is
unprivileged.
.TP
.B status [\-\-json]
Show active rules, selection, cache freshness and boot persistence. This
command is unprivileged.
.TP
.B block POP...
Make the listed POPs blocked and apply the result. In allow-only mode this
removes them from the allow list.
.TP
.B unblock POP...
Make the listed POPs allowed and apply the result. In allow-only mode this adds
them to the allow list.
.TP
.B only POP... [\-\-force]
Allow only the listed POPs; every other known POP is blocked. An empty
selection is refused unless \fB\-\-force\fR is given; forcing an empty
allow-list blocks every known POP.
.TP
.B preset [NAME] [\-\-list] [\-\-save] [\-\-delete]
Apply a preset, list presets, save the current selection under
\fINAME\fR, or delete \fINAME\fR.
.TP
.B refresh
Fetch a fresh SDR relay list and re-apply the saved selection unless paused.
.TP
.B apply
Apply the saved selection again. Unlike the boot service, a plain apply clears
the paused state.
.TP
.B pause
Remove the firewall rules while keeping the saved selection and presets. The
boot service skips applying while paused.
.TP
.B resume
Re-apply the saved selection after a pause.
.TP
.B clear
Remove the firewall rules and empty the saved selection. Presets are kept.
.TP
.B ping [POP...] [\-\-region REGION] [\-\-timeout SECONDS] [\-\-json]
Send unprivileged ICMP probes to relay addresses. This is an ICMP latency
hint, not Valve's SDR latency.
.TP
.B counters [\-\-json] [\-\-watch] [\-\-interval SECONDS]
Show per-POP drop counters published by the monitor service. This command is
unprivileged.
.TP
.B doctor [\-\-json] [\-\-privileged]
Run diagnostic checks. \fB\-\-privileged\fR runs the checks that need root
access.
.TP
.B persistence enable|disable
Enable or disable boot persistence.
.TP
.B version
Print the installed version.
.SH PRIVILEGES
Commands that write configuration, state or firewall rules require root. When
run as a normal user, they re-execute through \fBpkexec\fR by default. Use
\fB\-\-sudo\fR to force \fBsudo\fR, or run the installed helper directly as root.
.PP
The unprivileged commands are \fBlist\fR, \fBstatus\fR, \fBping\fR,
\fBcounters\fR, \fBdoctor\fR without \fB\-\-privileged\fR, and
\fBversion\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/cs2blocker/config.json
Root-owned selection and presets, written only by the helper.
.TP
.I /var/lib/cs2blocker/sdr-730.json
Root-owned cached SDR relay list.
.TP
.I /var/lib/cs2blocker/state.json
Last apply, refresh and pause state.
.TP
.I /run/cs2blocker/status.json
Live counters and backend status published by the monitor service.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B cs2blockctl list \-\-region Europe
List European POPs.
.TP
.B sudo cs2blockctl only sto sto2
Allow only the two Stockholm POPs and apply.
.TP
.B sudo cs2blockctl pause
Remove the current rules but preserve the saved selection.
.TP
.B cs2blockctl counters \-\-watch
Follow the live per-POP counters.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nft (8),
.BR pkexec (1),
.BR sudo (8),
.BR systemctl (1)
.PP
Project documentation:
